<section xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude" xml:id="sec-incremental-development">
  <title>Implementing Basic Algorithms</title>
  <introduction>
  <p>In Computer Science, an <term>algorithm</term> is a set of precise instructions to follow to perform a computation.
  You might rightly think this sounds a lot like a program, and it should. The difference is that an 
  algorithm is not written in a programming language. Instead, it's written in a human language, 
  like English, but meant to be unambiguous in its meaning. It can be helpful to write 
  an algorithm before writing a short program so that you have an understanding of the logic
  of your program before you start writing Java. This is especially important if you're 
  learning programming for the first time. Below is an example of applying this approach.</p>
  </introduction>


  <xi:include  href="subsec-rounding-ex.ptx"/>
</section>
